OL,3,GNEWSAMother whose newborn died after
OL,4,Afailed hospital checks was 'terrified
OL,5,Aand alone'
OL,6,
OL,7,FA mother whose newborn baby died after
OL,8,Fhospital staff failed to wake her for
OL,9,Fchecks before he was born told an
OL,10,Finquest she felt "terrified and alone".
OL,12,FEve Taylor, 29, was admitted to Ysbyty
OL,13,FGwynedd, Bangor, after her waters broke
OL,14,Fearly at 36 weeks and was identified as
OL,15,Fhaving signs of potential infection.
OL,17,FShe was due to be monitored again later
OL,18,Fthat night, but a midwife decided not
OL,19,Fto wake her up. Taylor awoke hours
OL,20,Flater and was rushed for an emergency
OL,21,FC-section.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
